WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.817
Sometimes we need more than two outcomes.

00:00:02.817 --> 00:00:06.262
Elif lets us test several rules in order.

00:00:06.262 --> 00:00:12.942
With a score of eighty-six, the first condition—score at least ninety—is false.

00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:21.737
Python then checks score at least eighty, which is true, so it prints “Good” and stops checking the remaining branches.

00:00:22.453 --> 00:00:25.735
Order matters because the first true branch wins.

00:00:25.735 --> 00:00:31.725
For threshold categories, it is often easiest to check from the highest threshold downward.

00:00:31.725 --> 00:00:36.370
Try scores of ninety-five, eighty-five, seventy-five, and sixty.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:41.196
Trace which branch should run before executing the code.
